--   Riemann–Hurwitz library, file 03: ring maps between the charts of K and L, the different divisor diffDiv, riemannHurwitz
-- statement:
--   Part 3 of 3 of a library proving the Riemann–Hurwitz formula with the different (wild ramification allowed) for an extension $L/K$ of algebraic function fields over a finite field $\mathbb{F}_q$: $2g_L - 2\ell_L(0) = [L:K](2g_K - 2\ell_K(0)) + \deg \mathrm{Diff}(L/K)$, with the different taken from Mathlib's `differentIdeal` on the finite chart (integral closure of $\mathbb{F}_q[x]$) and the infinite chart (integral closure of the valuation ring at $x = \infty$), without completions. Imports `Def_RPLib_FX_GOSB_02` and `Def_RPLib_S3_RRC`. Contents, in dependency order:
--
--   * the ring maps $R_K \to R_L$ and $R_K^\infty \to R_L^\infty$ between the integral closures of $\mathbb{F}_q[x]$ and of $\mathcal{O}_\infty$ in $K$ and in $L$, with their scalar-tower, integrality and torsion-freeness instances;
--   * the cotrace `ffCotrace` of $L/K$ and the different divisor `diffDiv` (finite part from `differentIdeal` of $R_L/R_K$, infinite part from `differentIdeal` of $R_L^\infty/R_K^\infty$);
--   * `RamanujanPetersson.GOS.riemannHurwitz`: $2 g_L - 2 \ell_L(0) = [L:K] (2 g_K - 2 \ell_K(0)) + \deg \mathrm{Diff}(L/K)$.
-- source:
--   H. Stichtenoth, Algebraic Function Fields and Codes, 2nd ed., GTM 254, Springer 2009, Sections 3.4-3.5; J. Neukirch, Algebraic Number Theory, Springer 1999, Chapter III.2 (the different)

